---
title: Razorbill
---
# Razorbill

The razorbill is a black-and-white auk of the north Atlantic with a deep, blunt
bill crossed by a white line. It takes sandeels and sprats while submerged,
propelling itself through the water with half-folded wings, and will work a
hundred metres below the surface when the shoals are deep. The single egg is
sharply pointed at one end and laid on a bare ledge, where its shape makes it
roll in a tight arc rather than off the rock. See [[alcidae]].
